# 6. Infinity, NaNs, and sign bit
6.1 Infinity arithmetic
  no exceptions generated, including:
	― add(inf, x), add(x, inf), sub(inf, x), sub(x, inf), for finite x
	― mul(inf, x), mul(x, inf), for finite or infinite x != 0
	― div(inf, x), div(x, inf), for finite x
	― squareRoot(+inf)
	― rem(x, inf) for finite normal x
	― conversion inf into inf in another format
  exceptions generated only when
	― inf is an invalid operand (see 7.2)
	― inf is created from finite operands by Ov (see 7.4) or Div0 (see 7.3)
	― rem(subnormal, inf) signals Underflow

